  "description": "The re-answers15 answers. CS5: InitiateSituation answers false for a null advice and for the advice already active, and false with status 5 (the popup posted without a vehicle, the advice still held) when a target mission finds no target or a coverage mission cannot build its cells; without a briefing a started mission answers true with status 5 [quirk]. CS9: a success without an active automaton has its effect and aura at (0, 0); a failure without an automaton or a target skips the effect, the aura and the money. CS10: 0xB on the active automaton marks it disabled and fails the mission at any status; a disabled target of a type-1 mission moves to the next target (the index and count stay), and with none left the mission succeeds. CS7: the track list is sorted ascending by advice priority (stable). CS11: slot 21 starts the advice in the first drivable automaton of the group in token order (or a created one, released after); slot 23 goes through slot 21 for the first entry whose advice accepts the group; slot 24 stores b, sends 0xABBBCA64 with no advice and enters the drive view; slot 25 sets the group and runs HandleInsertAutomaton.",
